{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-05 parser/help refinement approved and researched against current `origin/main` (`3b34d8b449ae4b56a5da8fb434aa75df7194b0c4`). Current `docs/cli-reference.md` is generated, but its syntax authority is not: `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` embeds 54 hand-maintained package-help files plus a curated 22-command intercept table and regex-parses the facade. It detects census drift, not parser/help drift. Source census found reusable argparse construction in only a minority of command families (`_bridge_commands`, `_jira_onboard`, `_llm_commands`, `_llm_eval_commands`, `_workflow_commands`, and six standalone command modules); most core ticket/store handlers still parse argv imperatively.\n\nApproved exact mechanism: every command grammar moves to a side-effect-free stdlib argparse factory; runtime handlers and the help generator call that same factory. Existing argparse builders are extracted. Imperative parsers migrate with accepted/rejected argv, double-dash handling, diagnostics, streams, and exit codes pinned by production-path compatibility tests. A narrow shared `ArgumentParser` subclass/formatter may preserve Rebar diagnostics; there is no docs-only parser, source-regex grammar, Click dependency, or second parser. Parser factories live in lean modules and accept a deterministic `prog`; generation alone resolves all factory refs, uses fixed formatting, and commits package-help/overview bytes. Runtime help remains a package-data read before RP-04 snapshot/config/mount/handler/optional imports.\n\nAliases do not duplicate grammar: exact aliases reuse canonical artifacts; bridge compatibility forms compose the same argument-definition helpers with alias-specific `prog` and replacement epilog; `jira-onboard` keeps its historical spelling; hidden `bridge-status` stays explicitly helpable but undiscoverable; `purge-bridge` stays unknown. The top-level lexical selector only identifies the command and first-token help/unknown forms, so it is routing rather than a competing argument grammar. Curated explanations/examples may remain editorial, but syntax/option tables must be generated or mechanically cross-checked.\n\nPrior art inspected at current upstream heads supports the same-source model: CPython argparse uses the same parser actions for `parse_args()` and `format_help()`; Django `BaseCommand.create_parser()` feeds both `print_help()` and `run_from_argv()`; Click derives parsing/help from one parameter graph; Cobra Markdown docs walk the execution command tree. Sources: https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/main/Lib/argparse.py ; https://github.com/django/django/blob/main/django/core/management/base.py ; https://github.com/pallets/click/blob/main/src/click/core.py ; https://github.com/spf13/cobra/blob/main/doc/md_docs.go .\n\nMigration is expand/contract by command family: each factory lands with its handler switched to it and behavioral parity tests. Generated artifacts become authoritative only when the complete registry/parser census passes, preventing a shipped docs-only grammar. Code and generated artifacts roll back together; no persisted data changes. Local detail appended to `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.joe-janitor/rp05-cli-registry-research.md`. No production or tracked file changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787070295307448001,"uuid":"e0eef28e-00f0-4536-b130-9919328a42a7"}